# Bentley OS — Architecture & Roadmap

*Source of truth pulled directly from `bentleylujero/bentley-os` @ main, plus local
uncommitted work as of 2026-07-10. Regenerate this doc from the repo whenever it
drifts — don't hand-edit it into staleness.*

---

## 1. System map — who does what

One `docker-compose.yml`, two networks (`backend` for services, `monitoring` for
ops tooling). Every service below has exactly one job. **If a new feature doesn't
obviously belong to one row, that's the sign to stop and decide before coding —
don't let it leak into two services.**

| Service | Port | Owns | Does NOT own |
|---|---|---|---|
| **postgres** | 5432 (LAN only) | All persisted state — ontology, sync tokens, audit log | Vector search (that's qdrant) |
| **qdrant** | 6333 (LAN only) | Vector storage for embeddings (Milestone 3+) | Currently **unused** — nothing writes to it yet |
| **redis** | 6379 (LAN only) | Caching / ephemeral state | Not used by any service yet either |
| **api** | 3000 | HTTP surface: `/health`, dashboard (`/`), ingestion (gcal/gmail — writes to Postgres), OpenCode proxy (`/opencode/*`) | Build/deploy logic, AI reasoning/classification |
| **deploy** | 4000 | Build + restart + health-check + auto-rollback for `api`, `opencode`, `marionette`; writes every action to `audit_log` | Anything about *what* code does — purely a CI/CD-style operator |
| **opencode** (container) | 4100 | **Stub only right now** — health check stub, target of the in-progress containerization effort | Not yet doing real work — see §3 duplication warning |
| **marionette** | 4200 | Future home of the `/think` AI agent (classification, morning brief, grounded Q&A) — currently a health-check stub | Ingestion (that's api's job), deploy (that's deploy's job) |
| **cloudflared** | — | Public tunnel, gated on `api` health | — |
| **portainer / dozzle / uptime-kuma** | 9000 / 8080 / 3001 | Ops visibility (containers, logs, uptime) | Nothing app-level |

**Rule of thumb going forward:** ingestion and read APIs live in `api`; AI
reasoning lives in `marionette`; anything that touches `docker compose` or git
lives in `deploy`. If a task description mentions two of these, split the ticket.

