## 4. Known bug already logged: rollback scope

`deploy/src/runner.ts`, in the rollback path:

```ts
await run(job, 'git', ['checkout', job.fromCommit, '--', '.']);
```

The `-- .` scopes the checkout to **the entire repo**, not the one service
that failed. A rollback triggered by a broken `api` deploy will also silently
revert any uncommitted-but-pushed changes to `marionette`, `opencode`, or
`deploy` itself sitting in that commit range. Must be scoped to the service's
own directory (e.g. `apps/api/`) before Milestone 5/6 turn on unattended
deploys — an autonomous system rolling back the wrong files with no one
watching is the failure mode this whole tiering exercise exists to prevent.

