**Done when:** events + emails land in Postgres on their own, with provenance.

### Milestone 2 — Insight out
Replace `apps/api/src/routes/dashboard.ts` (currently a static status card) with
server-rendered views reading `calendar_events` / `emails` directly. "Today"
and "what changed" first. Only reach for a separate frontend app if the
server-rendered version genuinely can't keep up.

### Milestone 3 — AI layer, read-only
Lives in **marionette**, not api. Email classification writes to the
already-existing `category`/`importance` columns. This is also where the
qdrant/embeddings decision can no longer be deferred — nothing currently
writes vectors anywhere.

### Milestone 4 — Action layer, approval-gated
New action types (create event, draft reply) behind one-click approval, all
writes going through `audit_log` — the same table `deploy` already uses, so
the audit trail is unified across "code changed" and "AI acted" from day one.

### Milestone 5 — Earned autonomy
Blocked on the rollback-scope fix in §4. Don't flip auto-execution on before
that's resolved — the blast radius of a bad auto-rollback is the same
mechanism that would need to contain a bad AI action.

### Milestone 6 — Self-extension
Tool registry + isolated test + approval + git automation + rollback, reusing
`deploy`'s existing job/audit machinery rather than building a second
build-and-rollback system next to it.

